{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And when you reap.</b> Rashi, of blessed memory, wrote: He repeated it to them so as to transgress two negative commandments. R. Avdimi bar R. Yossi said: What did the verse see to place them in the middle of the festivals? Passover and Shavuot on this side, Rosh HaShanah, Yom HaKippurim, and the Festival (Sukkot) on that side — this teaches you that whoever gives leket (gleanings), shikheḥah (forgotten produce), and pe'ah (corner) to the poor as is fitting, Scripture accounts it for him as though he built the Holy Temple and offered sacrifices within it. ״אני ה׳ אלהיכם״ — trustworthy to pay reward."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:50.933507022Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}